<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 420 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 420 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 420 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.4 BLN    1.5 BLN    1.5 BLN    1.5 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    675 MLN!   685 MLN    880 MLN*   1.3 BLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS				 195 MLN*</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   200 MLN*   10 MLN*    =	    =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE	 =	  =	    420 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 475 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING OCTOBER 21 AT 5-23/32 PCT</p>
<p>(INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
